                <invention-title lang="de">VERFAHREN UND VORRICHTUNG ZUR VIDEOCODIERUNG ZUR ABLEITUNG AFFINER BEWEGUNGSVEKTOREN FÜR CHROMAKOMPONENTEN</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">PROCÉDÉS ET APPAREIL DE CODAGE VIDÉO POUR DÉRIVER DES VECTEURS DE MOUVEMENT AFFINE POUR DES COMPOSANTES DE CHROMINANCE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">METHODS AND APPARATUS OF VIDEO CODING FOR DERIVING AFFINE MOTION VECTORS FOR CHROMA COMPONENTS</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method for video decoding, comprising: receiving video data arranged in luma and chroma subblocks, having a color sampling format, wherein each chroma subblock corresponds to luma subblocks according to the color sampling format; deriving an affine motion vector for a chroma subblock; and predicting the chroma subblock; wherein corresponding luma subblocks are derived according to the color sampling format; wherein the averaging process uses motion vectors from different luma subblocks under different color sampling formats, wherein for 4:4:4, the average luma motion vector is the motion vector of one corresponding luma subblock, wherein indices are the same as indices of the chroma subblock, and for 4:2:2, the average luma motion vector is obtained by taking an average of the motion vectors of two corresponding luma subblocks, wherein vertical indices are the same as a vertical index of the chroma subblock.</p>
            </abstract>
